  "equipment_type": "Air handler (residential heat recovery ventilation)",
  "applies_to": "Vasco SAB RVU controller boards (models 0x52xx residential and 0x53xx Energy Plus) with protocol release 0x0006, manual 90.01.06.53.",
  "summary": "The SAB RVU board in Vasco D150 Compact and Energy Plus heat recovery units speaks Modbus RTU on its RS485 port (connector M19), using holding registers only. The map covers identification, the live machine state (temperatures, fan speeds, pressures, CO2, RH, alarms, run hours), the main parameters and the command block for on/off, mode, speed and external RH/CO2 values.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "The manual prints hexadecimal register addresses and the first block starts at 0x0000 (serial number), which only fits addresses sent as printed. Use the hex value directly: 0x0110 = register 272 on the wire."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "Protocol release 0x0006",
  "source": {
    "title": "SAB RVU Ventilation Unit - Manual Modbus Protocol (D150 Compact, Energy Plus ENY-P1/2/3/4)",
    "doc_number": "90.01.06.53",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://vasco.eu/files/downloads/manuel-modbus-protocol-energy-plus/90.01.06.53-Handleiding-Modbus-registers-SAB-RVU.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 2 serial settings, data types and word order, pp. 3-4 block 0-1, pp. 5-6 block 2, p. 6-7 block 3"
  },
  "notes": [
    "32-bit values use two registers with the most significant 16 bits first (data type table), so the hours counter is ABCD.",
    "Left out: the four float registers Rho 1-4 (0x0115-0x011B), because the type table states the word order only for 32-bit integers; the four weekly timer programs (blocks 4-7, 0x0400-0x0737) and block 8 time/date.",
    "Byte-type registers (0x0108-0x010A) carry their 8 bits in the most significant byte of the register.",
    "Out-of-range parameter writes are accepted but clipped to the allowed range."
  ],
